Titre$ C Y S T O D E R M A   -   Roy Watling & Evelyn Turbull, BFF 8:37. 1998.
Com$ Adaptée par Paul Bertéa – 12-09-2011

1,2 $ Spores completely blueing in Melzer's reagent (amyloid) $ Stirps Amianthinum $s"Stirps Amianthinum"
1,5 $ Spores non-amyloid or only amyloid in hilar zone

2,0 $ Cap and stem white with pink or pale lilaceous tinges; alkali (KOH) solutions hardly discolouring the round cells on the cap $ C. carcharias
2,0,N$ Syn.: Lepiota carcharias (Pers.) P. Karst., Ryssl. Hattsvamp. 14, 1874./// ICONONOGRAPHIE :///- Lange 15D;///- Konrad & Maublanc 237/1;///- M 84/2;///- Ricken 82/3;///- Loquin M. BSMF 67: 75,1951, fig. 4.
2,3 $ Cap shades of yellowish or reddish brown, coral or rust-colour and the round cells darkening distinctly in alkali; spores distinctly amyloid 

3,0 $ Spores 3.5-5/2.5-3.5 µm, subglobose to broadly ovoid; cap rusty or brick-red with saffron or tawny ochraceous margin $ C. simulatum
3,0,N$///ICONOGRAPHIE :///- TBMS 43: 222, 1960, figs 13-15, 285.
3,4 $ Spores ellipsoid, cylindric-ellipsoid or fusoid, greater than 5 µm in length; cap paler

4,0 $ Cap apricot or sienna with paler margin; gills and flesh concolorous with cap and stem; spores 6-7.5(-8)/3-3.5(-4 µm broad $ C. jasonis
4,0,N$///Synonymes :///Lepiota amianthina var. longispora Kiihn., Bull. Soc. Mycol. France S2:204, 1936;///C. amianthinum var. longisporum (Kilhn. ex Kilhn.) Singer & Smith in Pap. Michigan Acad. Sci. 30 (1944): 114, 1945;///Cystoderma longisporum (Kühn.) Heinem. & Thoen in Bull. Soc. Mycol. France 69: 16, 1973.
4,0 $ Cap saffron or yellowish cream; gills and flesh white; spores 4-6.5(-7)12.5-3.5 µm $ C. amianthinum
4,0,N$ Syn.: Lepiota amianthina (Scopoli: Fr.) P. Karst., Ryssl. Hattsvamp. 15, 1879.///ICONONOGRAPHIE :///- Lange 15C;///- M 84/1;///- Bresadola 37;///- Ricken 81/4;///- Loquin. BSMF 67:70, 1951, fig. 1.

5,0 $ Spores amyloid only at hilar end (examine carefully!); cap purplish red; gills white finally tinged rose $ C. superbum $s"Strips Superbum"
5,0,N$///Misident.:. Armillaria haematites (Berk. & Broome) Sacc. s. Bres. non Berk. & Broome;///. Lepiota haematites (Berk. & Broome) Ricken ss. Ricken non al;///. Cystoderma haematites (Berk. & Broome) Kühn. & Maire, ss. auct. gall., Singer;///. Collybia lilacea Quel. ss. Konrad & Maubl. non Quélet.///ICONONOGRAPHIE :///- Bresadola 49, haematites;///- Konrad & Maublanc 237/2, haematites & 202, lilacea;///- Ricken,Die Blätterpilze 328, haematites;///- Locquin M. BSMF 67: 79, 1951, haematites;///- Fungus 26:39, 1956, figs 1-6 & 28:47, 1958.
5,6 $ Spores totally non-amyloid; cap dark rusty tawny, brick-, coral- or rust-colour $ Stirps Granulosum $s"Stirps Granulosum"

6,0 $ Cap dark rusty tawny, brick-colour or cinnamon; marginal cystidia absent $ C. granulosum
6,0,N$ Syn.: Lepiota granulosa (Batsch: Fr.) S. F. Gray in Nat. Arr. Brit. PI. I: 602,1821./// ICONONOGRAPHIE :///- Lange 15E;///- Bresadola 599;///- Ricken 81/3;///- Loquin M. BSMF 67: 77,1951, fig. 5.
6,0 $ Cap coral- to rust-colour, rusty brick; marginal cystidia tapering with narrow lanceolate apex, often with crystals $ C. terrei
6,0,N $Syn.:///. Agaricus terrei Berk. & Broome in Ann. Mag. Nat. Hist. 4(6): 462, 1870;///. Lepiota cinnabarina (Alb. & Schw.: Secr.) P. Karst., Ryssl. Hattsvamp. 14, 1879;///. Cystoderma cinnabarinum (Alb. & Schw.: Fr.) Fayod in Ann. Sci Nat. (Bot.) Ser. VII 9: 351, 1889./// ICONONOGRAPHIE :///- Lange 15F;///- Konrad & Maublanc 238;///- Bresadola 36;///- Ricken 81/2;///- Loquin M. BSMF 67: 73, 1951, fig. 3.
